Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• `Year` : filter for the two comparison years (2012‑01‑01 and 2017‑01‑01) and, when needed, extract the four–digit year.  
• `GeoName` : restrict the study to Massachusetts counties by keeping only the rows whose value ends with “, MA”.  
• `GeoFIPS` : keep track of the FIPS code for each geographic region (optional but often handy in joins).  
• `Earnings_per_job_avg` : the metric whose increase we want to measure (difference 2017 – 2012).  

Typical conditions that will recur  
1. `WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'`  – Massachusetts only.  
2. `WHERE Year IN (DATE '2012‑01‑01', DATE '2017‑01‑01')`  – only the two target years.  
3. `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM Year)=2012` (or 2017) – alternative year filtering.  
4. `WHERE Earnings_per_job_avg IS NOT NULL` – safety check when needed.  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final queries (all limited to 20 rows for demonstration).  
Replace or remove the LIMIT clause when a complete result set is desired.

```sql
--Description: 1) List 20 distinct Massachusetts county names found in the table.
SELECT DISTINCT GeoName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show the distinct DATE values stored in the Year column.
SELECT DISTINCT Year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
ORDER BY Year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show 2012 earnings‑per‑job averages for the first 20 MA counties.
SELECT GeoName,
       Earnings_per_job_avg
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND Year = DATE '2012-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Show 2017 earnings‑per‑job averages for the same counties.
SELECT GeoName,
       Earnings_per_job_avg
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND Year = DATE '2017-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Put the two years side‑by‑side with conditional aggregation (first 20 counties).
SELECT GeoName,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2012,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
GROUP BY GeoName
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Same as #5, but add the computed increase and order descending.
SELECT GeoName,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2012,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2017,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) -
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS increase_2012_to_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
GROUP BY GeoName
ORDER BY increase_2012_to_2017 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Retrieve the same information but also include GeoFIPS.
SELECT GeoFIPS,
       GeoName,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2012,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2017,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) -
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS increase_2012_to_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
GROUP BY GeoFIPS, GeoName
ORDER BY increase_2012_to_2017 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Use a self‑join instead of conditional aggregation to compute the increase.
SELECT a.GeoFIPS,
       a.GeoName,
       a.Earnings_per_job_avg AS earnings_2012,
       b.Earnings_per_job_avg AS earnings_2017,
       b.Earnings_per_job_avg - a.Earnings_per_job_avg AS increase_2012_to_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS b
  ON a.GeoFIPS = b.GeoFIPS
WHERE a.GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND a.Year = DATE '2012-01-01'
  AND b.Year = DATE '2017-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Same self‑join, but show only counties whose increase exceeded $5,000 and order by GeoName.
SELECT a.GeoName,
       b.Earnings_per_job_avg - a.Earnings_per_job_avg AS increase_2012_to_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS b
  ON a.GeoFIPS = b.GeoFIPS
WHERE a.GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND a.Year = DATE '2012-01-01'
  AND b.Year = DATE '2017-01-01'
  AND (b.Earnings_per_job_avg - a.Earnings_per_job_avg) > 5000
ORDER BY a.GeoName
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final answer – the increase in average earnings per job between 2012 and 2017 for every MA county.
SELECT GeoFIPS,
       GeoName,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2012,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2017,
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) -
       MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS increase_2012_to_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
  AND Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
GROUP BY GeoFIPS, GeoName
ORDER BY increase_2012_to_2017 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query (#10) is the one you would normally run without the `LIMIT` clause to get the complete list of Massachusetts counties, showing the 2012 value, the 2017 value, and the computed increase in average earnings per job.
